WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.997
Every kind of change takes one of five
lanes, and the lane settles three things:

2
00:00:04.997 --> 00:00:08.862
who approves, what actually runs,
and what evidence comes out.

3
00:00:08.862 --> 00:00:10.738
Two lanes run on machines.

4
00:00:10.738 --> 00:00:15.751
The gated lane, where a named person
approves each instance, is the default.

5
00:00:15.751 --> 00:00:18.243
The autonomous lane is only for narrow,

6
00:00:18.243 --> 00:00:23.463
low-risk classes the authorizing official
has accepted in writing, ahead of time.

7
00:00:23.463 --> 00:00:27.625
Then there's a human-decision lane, a
protocol lane with no ticket at all,

8
00:00:27.625 --> 00:00:30.999
and the declared exception
for when no machine can reach.

9
00:00:30.999 --> 00:00:33.587
Remember, this is the program's design.

10
00:00:33.587 --> 00:00:35.280
So which changes land where?
